s (for using them in a chronicle) and <i>something</i> clicked on my head...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:28:59-08:00","id":4005,"title":"","content":"Well, it's definitely inspired by the whole Cthulhu cycle and Elder Gods mythos, and it's vague enough so that it can be whatever the story requires. But as to a canon explanation...<br /> <br /> Given that we've got everything from the <i>Wraith</i> setting, at least until <i>Wraith20</i>, and the entire cosmology of the cWoD, I'm going to have to go with a hybrid theory: the Wyrm-as-Cthulhu. If the Umbra is like an onion, which is like an ogre, and has layers, then maybe it's the Wyrm breaking through the, I don't know, more &quot;spiritual&quot; side of the Dark Umbra and manifesting in the Tempest?<br /> <br /> Though I'm also intrigued by your Demon idea.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:48:33-08:00","id":5618,"title":"","content":"<br /> I have always viewed the Kraken as a manifestation of the Wyrm from Werewolf specifically the Eater of Souls who was banished by the Croatan and forced into a form of slumbering death. My support for this is Past Lives and the bane that is the central villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T01:33:29-08:00","id":5772,"title":"","content":"We were a few people on the old forum who did a fanbook project about abyss mysticism, in our research the mysterious Kraken also popped up. We tried to decide if it could be linked to abyss mysticism or not so we had to try to find everything WW had written about the creature. Here is what we found:<br /> Children of the Revolution says it's summoned from the void of the ocean depths and is described as a nightmarish monstrosity. It has umbrageous tentacles and is large and powerful enough to overwhelm six ships at the same time. It also feeds on blood.<br /> The Second Edition of Clanbook Giovanni says that the premascines supposedly can summon the Kraken. It hints that the Kraken actually is dead or undead.<br /> Blood Dimmed Tides says that it's also known by the names Qyrl, Dagon and the Tentacled One. It is the mother or father of all spineless ocean life. It was once worshipped on land as a God and awaits the time when it can return to land and godhood again. It is known as a creature of corruption and malevolence. It's vaster than an island and impossibly old and primordial. It's believed by the Lupines to be the undersea equivalent of all the corruption and evil, and is said to have a fierce rivalry with the undersea equivalent of Gaia.<br /> An ofc Wraith reports the monster to be older than most of the known underworld. It has never been seen in its entirety by any ghost but is said to have multiple tentacles as well as a single bloated eye in a rotting socket. It seems to be stuck on the other side of the Tempest but occasionally reaches through to the realm of ghosts. It is said to have an isatiable hunger. It is believed by some to be Oblivion itself or a forgotten diety attempting a belligerent return. Its possibly a threat to the Malfeans who are grateful it hasn't manifested fully in their Realm/Plane.<br /> <br /> I personally think that the Kraken swims all over the place, through all different layers/planes/realms and has some way to make its way to our &quot;real&quot; ocean depths. It probably reaches our ocean through the abyss realm (in vampire) since the abyss has some unsolved relationship with the lightless depths of our ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/629-anda","name":"anda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T13:00:38-08:00","id":6268,"title":"","content":"Not a fan of Exalted, but didn't it have a version in that game? Also, I think it also shows up in the last Orpheus book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T09:36:02-08:00","id":6885,"title":"","content":"by the way, if it's <i>something</i> from the Abyss.... it could be the Abyss itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].sty