thing specific to Wraith... it's it's own specter of a bygone creature. I'm gonna hafta agree with anda on the cross realms personification of all the terrifying mysteriousness of the ocean depths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T12:47:43-08:00","id":20305,"title":"","content":"The cross-dimensional personification of corruption is pretty darn cool!<br /> I've toyed with the idea of using the Kraken several times in both Vampire and Wraith but never got around to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T18:34:55-08:00","id":20453,"title":"","content":"For some reason I think of the Kraken as being something similar to the Gmork from the Neverending story... sort of an ultimate, bestial servant of Oblivion. I think to try to classify it as anything other than itself kind of makes it less... The Kraken is the Kraken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T05:57:16-07:00","id":526546,"title":"","content":"The idea of it being a forgotten deity chimes with the idea of Grandmother being God's twin, and as Oblivion being a dead universe. If the fragmented paradigm model is true, the Kraken (which intrudes upon several different layers of reality), could be related to Grandmother/Oblivion. Like Grandmother, the Kraken could be another manifestation of Oblivion. And Oblivion could be the Dark Umbral reflection/intrusion of an aspect of the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:24:24-07:00","id":526852,"title":"","content":"I've always just gone with the Kraken as being something that &quot;Just is&quot; I've really seen no great need for its explanation for why and what it is. Its already got a name and adding history names it too much.<br /> <br /> From what I recall Wyrm and Oblivion are two very separate entities. Wyrm being an active destructive force and Oblivion being passive. Such so that if the Wyrm were to &quot;win&quot; Oblivion is what would ultimately consume the last of the Triad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:27:58-07:00","id":526853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken#post2699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Creatures from the Outer Space (<u>from the Outer Space</u>): Doing it just because it's fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> All the Cthulhu-esque assumptions are contained in the point 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its all fun and games until Cthulhu calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:02:36-07:00","id":527012,"title":"","content":"The Kraken.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nzx_yqU1ZGw?t=17m18s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nzx_yqU1ZGw?t=17m18s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nzx_yqU1ZGw?t=17m18s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/nzx_yqU1ZGw?t=17m18s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:42:57-07:00","id":527229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An ofc Wraith reports the monster to be older than most of the known underworld. </div> </div> </div>So it was likely around when the War between the Angels and Demons was occuring then? Makes sense, given what else is known about it. In real life, it seems to stem from a late 13th century Old Icelandic saga, as a legendary fictional beast. There likely have been stories dating before that of larger sea-creatures, likely going under other names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T13:07:47-07:00","id":528032,"title":"","content":"There probably are beings in the Underworld sorta who know. I believe it's mentioned that if you used the Labyrinth, you could head out Moon-wards and there you'd find weird ghost... things older than humanity both from Earth and not of it ever. Along those lines, you could think of it as something that squeezed its way through the Labyrinth and surfaced in the Tempest. Which then has some cool imagery of a pair of giant whirlpools... one flowing down into the Labyrinth... and more terrifyingly one flowing UP from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T10:09:26-07:00","id":530092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=528032#post528032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There probably are beings in the Underworld sorta who know. I believe it's mentioned that if you used the Labyrinth, you could head out Moon-wards and there you'd find weird ghost... things older than humanity both from Earth and not of it ever. Along those lines, you could think of it as something that squeezed its way through the Labyrinth and surfaced in the Tempest. Which then has some cool imagery of a pair of giant whirlpools... one flowing down into the Labyrinth... and more terrifyingly one flowing UP from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, THIS is really interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T01:50:16-07:00","id":531795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=528032#post528032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There probably are beings in the Underworld sorta who know. I believe it's mentioned that if you used the Labyrinth, you could head out Moon-wards and there you'd find weird ghost... things older than humanity both from Earth and not of it ever. Along those lines, you could think of it as something that squeezed its way through the Labyrinth and surfaced in the Tempest. Which then has some cool imagery of a pair of giant whirlpools... one flowing down into the Labyrinth... and more terrifyingly one flowing UP from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe that moving through the Labyrinth, one could potentially outwards through the Lower Umbra and reach Malfeas in the Deep Universe. I like the link of the Umbra to Malfeas as a Primordial Realm and it links nicely being the prison of the Wyrm. Just how the Kraken could link to either, neither or perhaps if you so wanted... <i>Yozi</i> (for those who still like their link to Exalted) would make for a fun venture, especially in crossover games or a particularly adventurous (perhaps suicidal) Doomslayer wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T12:22:26-07:00","id":532114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=527012#post527012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kraken.<br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/nzx_yqU1ZGw?t=17m18s\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/nzx_yqU1ZGw?t=17m18s</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that goes back a bit. The production value holds up. Too bad the writing wasn't better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T14:04:36-07:00","id":532263,"title":"","content":"It was pretty effective at giving six-year-old me nightmares for weeks on end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T01:42:18-07:00","id":540778,"title":"","content":"I'm currently thinking of having the Kraken as a Malfean Neverborn soul. One of the Exalted ones, rather than the Mage Nephandi ones... Given the original link the books had. Also that the Kraken seems analogous to the underwater aspect of Gaia, she was a Primordial herself in Exalted, with numerous souls too and as such she likely has one as her underwater aspect to match the Kraken as discussed in page.1 of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T02:02:34-07:00","id":552760,"title":"","content":"My Guess is Mage20 is going to chuck everything to do with Demon: the Fallen, since Demon kinda took away a lot of Wraith's metaplot. Making Charon an Angel was kinda stupid in my own opinion.<br /> <br /> I also don't like to think of the Kraken as being related to Demons or the Wyrm...It takes away from the uniqueness of Wraith by having one of it's signature strange creatures be dependent upon another gameline. Besides, Oblivion is more powerful than the Wyrm anyway, and will devour it when/if the Wyrm wins in the first place.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Kraken being mysterious, an entity older than all of humanity, some undead great beast from the primordial state of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T23:03:33-07:00","id":553956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=552760#post552760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Guess is Mage20 is going to chuck everything to do with Demon: the Fallen, since Demon kinda took away a lot of Wraith's metaplot. Making Charon an Angel was kinda stupid in my own opinion.<br /> <br /> I also don't like to think of the Kraken as being related to Demons or the Wyrm...It takes away from the uniqueness of Wraith by having one of it's signature strange creatures be dependent upon another gameline. Besides, Oblivion is more powerful than the Wyrm anyway, and will devour it when/if the Wyrm wins in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't start that sort of thing if you don't want to get drawn into a lengthy and ultimately aimless discussion about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:19:13-07:00","id":554007,"title":"","content":"this whole charon being an angel thing is a misunderstanding. the idea is that there was some angel that was called charon with the implication that the lade of fate named the wraith we know as charon that way in order to give him some power of the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:33:21-07:00","id":554274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=554007#post554007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this whole charon being an angel thing is a misunderstanding. the idea is that there was some angel that was called charon with the implication that the lade of fate named the wraith we know as charon that way in order to give him some power of the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still fits in the same territory, since there's no indication through Wraith that the &quot;prior Charon&quot; existed or was important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-14-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:28:07-07:00","id":554615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=554274#post554274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still fits in the same territory, since there's no indication through Wraith that the &quot;prior Charon&quot; existed or was important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly, Demon: The Fallen is a great game on it's own....But it REALLY fucks up every other game's setting except for Vampire and Hunter.<br /> <br /> It's why it's best to be ignored when talking about Wraith.<br /> <br /> Sadly, they could have named a Fallen who WOULD have fit in perfectly with Wraith.... Nuhadri... Charon just found Nuhadri in the Labryinth. No idea who he was, or where he came from, and yet the dude had the knowledge on how to smelt souls....If Demon had said &quot;There was a Slayer who created the Underworld and his name was Nuhadri&quot; that would have made everything click in a really cool way.<br /> <br /> Instead we had this cheapening which takes away from Wraith and how cool/important Charon was to the Underworld. Making him just some johnny come lately who put on a mask instead of &quot;The REAL Charon&quot; just sucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:23:25-07:00","id":554666,"title":"","content":"Actually Nuhadri exists iirc. I think it was in Houses of the Fallen. Should be the most prominent Annunaki of the Alabaster Legion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:47:51-07:00","id":555810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=554615#post554615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly, Demon: The Fallen is a great game on it's own....But it REALLY fucks up every other game's setting except for Vampire and Hunter.<br /> <br /> It's why it's best to be ignored when talking about Wraith.<br /> <br /> Sadly, they could have named a Fallen who WOULD have fit in perfectly with Wraith.... Nuhadri... Charon just found Nuhadri in the Labryinth. No idea who he was, or where he came from, and yet the dude had the knowledge on how to smelt souls....If Demon had said &quot;There was a Slayer who created the Underworld and his name was Nuhadri&quot; that would have made everything click in a really cool way.<br /> <br /> Instead we had this cheapening which takes away from Wraith and how cool/important Charon was to the Underworld. Making him just some johnny come lately who put on a mask instead of &quot;The REAL Charon&quot; just sucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wanting to get into a DtF vs. everything else &quot;discussion&quot; here, but.... <br /> <br /> Flinty's correct observation that the equivalency between Nhudri the First Artificer and Nhudri(el) the Annunaki is one of the great intrusions/cross-over points between DtF and WtO. WtO went out of it's way to leave Nhudri a mystery. He needed to be rescued from the Labyrinth, but he doesn't appear to be Shadow-Eaten. He knows how to forge soulsteel, but there isn't much of an explanation of how he knows this. (Which is a really really weird thing to know, since Charon comes from a Bronze Age culture, most wraiths older than him shouldn't have a clue how to forge ANTYTHING.) He was obviously in the Labyrinth before all the history of Stygia, the Far Shores, etc happened, so there is a question about what culture, location could have produced him. <br /> <br /> DtF resolves this by&quot;revealing&quot; that he is one of the Fallen. Which answers pretty much all those mysteries. As an angel, he predates pretty much all human cultures, the Abyss being below the Labyrinth it makes sense that Charon found him somewhere down &quot;there&quot;, being an Annunaki, he probably once exemplified something along the lines of forging, alloying, whatever so making soulsteel makes sense, etc. Of course this ADDS a bunch of new questions. Did Charon actually get into the Abyss? How? Just as importantly, how did he get out again with Nhudri and leave the seals intact? If Charon didn't get into the Abyss, how did Nhudri get out and into the Labyrinth? There is an EPIC story there. And an archetypical one. Going into Hell to rescue/claim one of the dead/damned resonates all over the place.<br /> <br /> Why is it cheap to take or be given the name of someone in the past who was great? Did it cheapen all the Emperors of the Roman Empire to go by the title &quot;Augustus&quot; after the first Emperor? Or, later on, &quot;Caesar&quot;? Did it cheapen Russia to have it's rulers go by Czar? Germany to have it's ruler go by Kaiser? The Lady of Fate may have been around when Charon was (since there are a few hints that she might be Eve). Even if not, she's got that whole oracle thing going and may have bestowed the name(/title) to indicate the legitimacy of his rule over the Underworld and/or to draw upon the sympathetic resonance associated with names to do so (probably both). It doesn't make Charon any the less cool for being Charon... it's all such ancient pre-history and he is so THERE that the name &quot;Charon&quot; doesn't mean anything other than HIM to anyone in Stygia (maybe a very very very few people). He OWNS the name now. It's not like it's his real name in any case, so there had to be some reason to take it on....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T16:59:10-07:00","id":556226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=555810#post555810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not wanting to get into a DtF vs. everything else &quot;discussion&quot; here, but....</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not possible. Mentioning Demon invokes it automatically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flinty's correct observation that the equivalency between Nhudri the First Artificer and Nhudri(el) the Annunaki is one of the great intrusions/cross-over points between DtF and WtO. WtO went out of it's way to leave Nhudri a mystery. He needed to be rescued from the Labyrinth, but he doesn't appear to be Shadow-Eaten. He knows how to forge soulsteel, but there isn't much of an explanation of how he knows this. (Which is a really really weird thing to know, since Charon comes from a Bronze Age culture, most wraiths older than him shouldn't have a clue how to forge ANTYTHING.) He was obviously in the Labyrinth before all the history of Stygia, the Far Shores, etc happened, so there is a question about what culture, location could have produced him.<br /> <br /> DtF resolves this by&quot;revealing&quot; that he is one of the Fallen. Which answers pretty much all those mysteries. As an angel, he predates pretty much all human cultures, the Abyss being below the Labyrinth it makes sense that Charon found him somewhere down &quot;there&quot;, being an Annunaki, he probably once exemplified something along the lines of forging, alloying, whatever so making soulsteel makes sense, etc. Of course this ADDS a bunch of new questions. Did Charon actually get into the Abyss? How? Just as importantly, how did he get out again with Nhudri and leave the seals intact? If Charon didn't get into the Abyss, how did Nhudri get out and into the Labyrinth? There is an EPIC story there. And an archetypical one. Going into Hell to rescue/claim one of the dead/damned resonates all over the place.<br /> <br /> Why is it cheap to take or be given the name of someone in the past who was great? Did it cheapen all the Emperors of the Roman Empire to go by the title &quot;Augustus&quot; after the first Emperor? Or, later on, &quot;Caesar&quot;? Did it cheapen Russia to have it's rulers go by Czar? Germany to have it's ruler go by Kaiser? The Lady of Fate may have been around when Charon was (since there are a few hints that she might be Eve). Even if not, she's got that whole oracle thing going and may have bestowed the name(/title) to indicate the legitimacy of his rule over the Underworld and/or to draw upon the sympathetic resonance associated with names to do so (probably both). It doesn't make Charon any the less cool for being Charon... it's all such ancient pre-history and he is so THERE that the name &quot;Charon&quot; doesn't mean anything other than HIM to anyone in Stygia (maybe a very very very few people). He OWNS the name now. It's not like it's his real name in any case, so there had to be some reason to take it on.... </div> </div> </div>It cheapens it to make it completely subsidiary to another line. Text doesn't matter here, only metatext; &quot;honoring&quot; angels from the continuity of Demon in this case is meaningless and worthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:02:05-07:00","id":556310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=555810#post555810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course this ADDS a bunch of new questions. Did Charon actually get into the Abyss? How? Just as importantly, how did he get out again with Nhudri and leave the seals intact? If Charon didn't get into the Abyss, how did Nhudri get out and into the Labyrinth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well going by Slayer lore a few scant members of the Alabaster Legion never got imprisoned and rather flew to a place below even Stygia. It is heavily hinted at them having become the fitfully sleeping Malfeans. Maybe Nhudriel was one of the Malfeans and with a bit helpf from either Charon or other forces supporting him got a bit of Faith infused into him (in the form of a substantial offering of Pathos), effectivly waking him up. The fact that the other Malfeans are effectivly seen as evil in Wraith lore COULD be misinformation (since they pretty much all sleep in the Labyrinth just atop the abyss which probably gives them all kinds of Nightmares, which in turn may manifest in weird ways). They are surely touched by the abyss thanks to their sleeping spot, however they did not get imprisoned and didn't feel the immense spiritual torture this accompanies. So if they wake they MAY not be Earthboud level crazy evil but may recover their minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:52:11-07:00","id":556360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=556310#post556310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well going by Slayer lore a few scant members of the Alabaster Legion never got imprisoned and rather flew to a place below even Stygia. It is heavily hinted at them having become the fitfully sleeping Malfeans. Maybe Nhudriel was one of the Malfeans and with a bit helpf from either Charon or other forces supporting him got a bit of Faith infused into him (in the form of a substantial offering of Pathos), effectivly waking him up. The fact that the other Malfeans are effectivly seen as evil in Wraith lore COULD be misinformation (since they pretty much all sleep in the Labyrinth just atop the abyss which probably gives them all kinds of Nightmares, which in turn may manifest in weird ways). They are surely touched by the abyss thanks to their sleeping spot, however they did not get imprisoned and didn't feel the immense spiritual torture this accompanies. So if they wake they MAY not be Earthboud level crazy evil but may recover their minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering how the need for a Relic or the like for an Earthbound applies/functions/etc. in the Shadowlands? Perhaps the Alabaster Legion didn't end up as Eartbound or Malfeans or Demons per se. Or how a Demon might become &quot;integrated&quot; into something other than a thing or person... Might Nhudri have joined with a wraith/specter? Not sure. DtF didn't get to the point of dealing with the other gaming lines on other than plot in most respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:04:43-07:00","id":556369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=556226#post556226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not possible. Mentioning Demon invokes it automatically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It cheapens it to make it completely subsidiary to another line. Text doesn't matter here, only metatext; &quot;honoring&quot; angels from the continuity of Demon in this case is meaningless and worthless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, of course. Exactly what I was saying. Just like how Werewolf's cosmology is a wrecking ball through the rest of the settings... So we have to have discussions about how the Wyrm is superior to Oblvivion or a part of it or it's a part of the Wyrm or whatever. Pick WtF for your fundamental truth if that is your poison (and it is a very pernicious poison indeed) or DtF if that's how you feel. Or say there is no one Truth and it all just matters on perspective... which might be the &quot;MtA supreme&quot; way... And so on and so on....<br /> <br /> But talking about how WtO and DtF fit together from the very limited intersection of a few aspects of the metaplot that weren't nailed down in WtO and were picked up as threads in a later game.... how on Earth does that render one line subsidiary to another? Especially since, without any evidence to the contrary so far, the connections you despise are definitely something that the people writing the games were at least okay with, if not totally cool about. <br /> <br /> Since I was named to honor my uncle and my grandfather and there is a tradition of using the same male name every other generation on my mother's side, I can TOTALLY see how it makes sense to honor someone with another person's name. In fact, after, &quot;it's pretty and what we could agree on&quot; it's probably the next major reason that people get named in modern America, judging from all the Juniors, III's etc I see all around me. Hopefully naming someone after their grandfather doesn't cheapen the name for either party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:30:01-07:00","id":556388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=556360#post556360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm wondering how the need for a Relic or the like for an Earthbound applies/functions/etc. in the Shadowlands? Perhaps the Alabaster Legion didn't end up as Eartbound or Malfeans or Demons per se. Or how a Demon might become &quot;integrated&quot; into something other than a thing or person... Might Nhudri have joined with a wraith/specter? Not sure. DtF didn't get to the point of dealing with the other gaming lines on other than plot in most respects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The remnant of the Alabaster Legion that fled to the depths of the Labyrinth were never imprisoned, so they have no need for a relic or person to posess - they are not affected by the pull of the abyss (like Lucifer in that regard). They are basically spirit beings who need the energy of faith or fall into powerless slumber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:00:24-07:00","id":556405,"title":"","content":"I like the stuff that Demon adds to the mythos of Wraith but also I feel at odds with things it changes too. Things like the original Fallen Angel named Charon (interesting, as is the Haven creation myth)... The Labyrinth being made by the original Charon as they dug ever downwards, I feel at odds with the mention in 1e Wraith in that it stemmed from the Malfeans digging <i>upwards</i> into the Seas to cause chaos in the times before Charon (the wraith). Still, myths and legends solves that, I suppose in that no wraith really would have been about in those days.<br /> <br /> In <i>my</i> Wraith setting, the mythos is still linked to the past of <i>Exalted</i>, so the Underworld stems from the Primordial War and the Malfeans are <i>the Malfeans</i> of that game. Yet, I do <i>love</i> the idea of Nhudri being an Angel, also the possibility of being a Neverborn too, through what become of his people. We know the War over Creation between the forces of God and Lucifer got pretty escalated at a point and soulforging could easily have been one of the horrific weapons used in those times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:36:29-07:00","id":556511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=556369#post556369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, yes, of course. Exactly what I was saying. Just like how Werewolf's cosmology is a wrecking ball through the rest of the settings... So we have to have discussions about how the Wyrm is superior to Oblvivion or a part of it or it's a part of the Wyrm or whatever. Pick WtF for your fundamental truth if that is your poison (and it is a very pernicious poison indeed) or DtF if that's how you feel. Or say there is no one Truth and it all just matters on perspective... which might be the &quot;MtA supreme&quot; way... And so on and so on....<br /> <br /> But talking about how WtO and DtF fit together from the very limited intersection of a few aspects of the metaplot that weren't nailed down in WtO and were picked up as threads in a later game.... how on Earth does that render one line subsidiary to another? Especially since, without any evidence to the contrary so far, the connections you despise are definitely something that the people writing the games were at least okay with, if not totally cool about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shoots the mystery that others were using dead. That's it, you can go home, that character was really a fallen angel! Nothing more to be done here with this shady area of canon, we're not using it anymore and it's getting shipped off to a different game.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's also worth noting that Demon arrived so late on the scene that it didn't have strong connections to any other game except possibly for Vampire, and that's only because of the Noddism railroad to the end of the line. There were still few, if any, mentions of it in other games. It burned out in a flash in just two years, and thus far, seems not to be present in any anniversary edition books, even as a potential thing for the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since I was named to honor my uncle and my grandfather and there is a tradition of using the same male name every other generation on my mother's side, I can TOTALLY see how it makes sense to honor someone with another person's name. In fact, after, &quot;it's pretty and what we could agree on&quot; it's probably the next major reason that people get named in modern America, judging from all the Juniors, III's etc I see all around me. Hopefully naming someone after their grandfather doesn't cheapen the name for either party. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't actually have much to do with the discussion. Real world family traditions aren't the game, and vice versa. I'm guessing that the original statement about cheapening the character had much more to do with stolen thunder, and not the practice of naming people after the relatives of the parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-16-2015, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T02:14:22-07:00","id":556697,"title":"","content":"i believe one book of dtf says that azrael the archduke fought of the elohim on order for his subordinates to escape to the labyrinth. so nuhadri did not need to be rescued.<br /> presumably the idea is that the rest of them became the neverborn. days of fire seems to support this calling them the not born.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:02:34-07:00","id":557228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=556697#post556697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i believe one book of dtf says that azrael the archduke fought of the elohim on order for his subordinates to escape to the labyrinth. so nuhadri did not need to be rescued.<br /> presumably the idea is that the rest of them became the neverborn. days of fire seems to support this calling them the not born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Days of Fire says a lot of things. The author noted that it was made for people to see what they want to see for their particular game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T16:24:09-07:00","id":557493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=556511#post556511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It shoots the mystery that others were using dead. That's it, you can go home, that character was really a fallen angel! Nothing more to be done here with this shady area of canon, we're not using it anymore and it's getting shipped off to a different game.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's also worth noting that Demon arrived so late on the scene that it didn't have strong connections to any other game except possibly for Vampire, and that's only because of the Noddism railroad to the end of the line. There were still few, if any, mentions of it in other games. It burned out in a flash in just two years, and thus far, seems not to be present in any anniversary edition books, even as a potential thing for the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This doesn't actually have much to do with the discussion. Real world family traditions aren't the game, and vice versa. I'm guessing that the original statement about cheapening the character had much more to do with stolen thunder, and not the practice of naming people after the relatives of the parents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tons of books shoot the mysteries of other lines dead. You must have HATED Orpheus with an incomparable loathing and obviously burned the the various end-times books to ash, then pissed on the ashes before burying them in an undisclosed location. (Err... probably should start in the undisclosed location...) And most of Hunter after the first books as well. Nothing but mystery shattering going on there. Ends of Empire, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, Nights of Prophecy, the Giovanni Chronicles, etc. etc. etc. etc. etc. (Oh, of course, some of those things are &quot;optional&quot;, but then so is everything for that matter and, specifically many of those options were put out there SPECIFICALLY to answer outstanding metaplot questions). <br /> <br /> Demon may not have had super strong sales, but that had a whole lot less to do with a two year run than the advent of NWOD. DtF was as much a victim of a corporate re-branding as, say, the remaining Convention books for Mage, a kithbook or so for Changeling, etc. Would it have lasted and grown? More likely than not it would have to some degree. It didn't have much of a chance. And, oh yeah, Hunter and Demon were definitely interlinked substantially on many different levels. Which is a lot more than &quot;possibly Vampire&quot; with the never-abadoned-always-critically-front-and-center importance of the its connection to the Caine mythos. That means DtF had connections with HtR, VtM, WtO. It was lacking much in the way of crossover with MtA or, particularly, WtA (with the whole &quot;What Umbra?&quot; thing in Demon). (In some ways it's easier to tie VtM, HtR, WtO, DtF, MtR together in a fairly coherent World of Darkness.... Mage and Werewolf are the odd ones out on several levels).<br /> <br /> If you are saying that reusing a name is cheap, there is no material difference between re-using a name in a family to honor elders/ancestors, picking a name of a respected/revered historical figure, or taking a part of a personal name and then turning it into a title for a the ruler of an Empire. They are all the same thing to different degrees. Charon - the Mycenaen traveller tapped by Fate posthumously to rule the Underworld being named for Charon - the angel who is responsible for the creation of said Underworld makes a lot of sense on many different levels, one which is the whole idea of persistence of memory that underpins the entire game of Wraith. Maybe he HAD to be renamed Charon to be able to tap into that rule to BE the ruler of the Underworld.... It's better than having to become/join up with a Malfean (I'm looking at you Qin Shi-Huand Di...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T21:39:30-07:00","id":557860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=557493#post557493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tons of books shoot the mysteries of other lines dead. You must have HATED Orpheus with an incomparable loathing and obviously burned the the various end-times books to ash, then pissed on the ashes before burying them in an undisclosed location. (Err... probably should start in the undisclosed location...) And most of Hunter after the first books as well. Nothing but mystery shattering going on there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one deserves special mention, because Orpheus basically was Wraith 2: Now With More Flatliners and Frighteners, so I don't really know why it would get listed here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ends of Empire </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that just Wraith's early exit prior to the Time of Judgment? A shame more than a hate target, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. I'm hardly unique on that count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nights of Prophecy, the Giovanni Chronicles, etc. etc. etc. etc. etc. (Oh, of course, some of those things are &quot;optional&quot;, but then so is everything for that matter and, specifically many of those options were put out there SPECIFICALLY to answer outstanding metaplot questions). </div> </div> </div>They produced a funny joke I made a while back about the anticlimactic and defeatist nature of Vampire metaplot, so there was that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon may not have had super strong sales, but that had a whole lot less to do with a two year run than the advent of NWOD. DtF was as much a victim of a corporate re-branding as, say, the remaining Convention books for Mage, a kithbook or so for Changeling, etc. Would it have lasted and grown? More likely than not it would have to some degree. It didn't have much of a chance. And, oh yeah, Hunter and Demon were definitely interlinked substantially on many different levels. </div> </div> </div>Major conflicts, there. One person writes Lucifer claiming to be responsible for Imbued, another writes him as having no clue where they came from. Down to the wire, down to the bone... about the only clear link there was involved an Earthbound that got capped off after inhabiting Leaf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is a lot more than &quot;possibly Vampire&quot; with the never-abadoned-always-critically-front-and-center importance of the its connection to the Caine mythos. That means DtF had connections with HtR, VtM, WtO. It was lacking much in the way of crossover with MtA or, particularly, WtA (with the whole &quot;What Umbra?&quot; thing in Demon). (In some ways it's easier to tie VtM, HtR, WtO, DtF, MtR together in a fairly coherent World of Darkness.... Mage and Werewolf are the odd ones out on several levels).<br /> <br /> If you are saying that reusing a name is cheap, there is no material difference between re-using a name in a family to honor elders/ancestors, picking a name of a respected/revered historical figure, or taking a part of a personal name and then turning it into a title for a the ruler of an Empire. </div> </div> </div>Not in fiction, no. The entire thing is a story of imagination. You can imagine more names easily, and you don't have to deal with the irritating, error-produced problem of Two Kuklas. It may be more of a concern for Exalted, given its history of rogue writers going against the developer, but in the end, it seems to arrive at a similar end point: a dire need for a retcon. Many retcons were furnished in revised, and often made the material healthier for it; Vic Stryker fits in better as a werewolf if his companions are a proper pack of other werewolves and not a Son of Ether mage and an Eshu changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are all the same thing to different degrees. Charon - the Mycenaen traveller tapped by Fate posthumously to rule the Underworld being named for Charon - the angel who is responsible for the creation of said Underworld makes a lot of sense on many different levels, one which is the whole idea of persistence of memory that underpins the entire game of Wraith. Maybe he HAD to be renamed Charon to be able to tap into that rule to BE the ruler of the Underworld.... It's better than having to become/join up with a Malfean (I'm looking at you Qin Shi-Huand Di...) </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of trying to come up with clever ways of tying together poorly considered material. Exalted 2e spoiled it for me, but again, as with DSotBH, not exactly a unique case, here. Why bother trying to come up with a rickety, twee setup when you can cut things down to a simpler, functional level as a base? People who are interested in constructing elaborate connections will probably do this on their own. I see the games as needing to stand on their own, because crossover did not historically produce much fun for me back in the days of second edition, and I don't want a repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T09:16:09-07:00","id":558325,"title":"","content":"That's all your opinion as a critic of the various lines. You are deciding which parts of the story are okay with you and which aren't Which is absolutely what you can do. Dislike them all you want. <br /> <br /> However, the metaplot IS one huge narrative (with space here and there for people's games to intersect on some level or avoid). It's not a great one as far as consistency goes, though it is a lot better than most people give it credit for. To critique the joins is fine, but it's not determinative or dispositive. If the metaplot saith &quot;Nhudri = Nhudriel. Charon the Ferryman/Emperor has the same name as an angel. The Abyss is related dimensionally to the Labyrinth. Etc. Thus endeth the connections, both narratively and in setting, between WtO and DtF&quot; then that's the way it is. In your game you can chose to ignore it or rewrite it. That's classic Golden Rule. If you do the later, you are veering off the metaplot path and might have to make adjustments and some adjustment may take you far enough off the path that the your game becomes disjoined from the metaplot. Which is largely intrinsic to CWOD games. It's one of the reasons people play them. There are lots of game systems out there with absolutely no metaplot and less to no story &quot;built in&quot; from the get go. <br /> <br /> However, this is going really really far afield from talking about big squid-y things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T20:21:34-07:00","id":559012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=558325#post558325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all your opinion as a critic of the various lines. You are deciding which parts of the story are okay with you and which aren't Which is absolutely what you can do. Dislike them all you want.<br /> <br /> However, the metaplot IS one huge narrative (with space here and there for people's games to intersect on some level or avoid). It's not a great one as far as consistency goes, though it is a lot better than most people give it credit for. To critique the joins is fine, but it's not determinative or dispositive. If the metaplot saith &quot;Nhudri = Nhudriel. Charon the Ferryman/Emperor has the same name as an angel. The Abyss is related dimensionally to the Labyrinth. Etc. Thus endeth the connections, both narratively and in setting, between WtO and DtF&quot; then that's the way it is. In your game you can chose to ignore it or rewrite it. That's classic Golden Rule. If you do the later, you are veering off the metaplot path and might have to make adjustments and some adjustment may take you far enough off the path that the your game becomes disjoined from the metaplot. Which is largely intrinsic to CWOD games. It's one of the reasons people play them. There are lots of game systems out there with absolutely no metaplot and less to no story &quot;built in&quot; from the get go.<br /> <br /> However, this is going really really far afield from talking about big squid-y things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 20th anniversary editions have basically taken the metaplot and chucked it into the sun. Vampire basically said &quot;Revised didn't happen&quot; Werewolf got rid of the red star, but did change the least... and Mage 20 is not only moving as and sweeping the whole Avatar Storm thing under the rug, but also flat-out made the Nephandus as the real over-arching villains of the game instead of the Technocracy. It also completely rejected the &quot;Technocracy Triumphant&quot; paradigm.<br /> <br /> I would hazard to guess Wraith20 is going to chuck the whole &quot;Charon was really an Angel&quot; development along with the rest of Demon's influences, and Wraith will be better all the for it. Hell, Stygia is going to exist along side of Orpheus in Wraith20... rather than being obliterated by the sixth great Maletstrom, somehow the Underworld is going to have weathered it.<br /> <br /> This is good news, because Revised was the era when while whitewolf put out some of their greatest works... but also had the stupidest cross-overs involving metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T11:19:21-07:00","id":559578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/2699-wraith-the-oblivion-ok-so-the-kraken?p=559012#post559012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The 20th anniversary editions have basically taken the metaplot and chucked it into the sun. Vampire basically said &quot;Revised didn't happen&quot; Werewolf got rid of the red star, but did change the least... and Mage 20 is not only moving as and sweeping the whole Avatar Storm thing under the rug, but also flat-out made the Nephandus as the real over-arching villains of the game instead of the Technocracy. It also completely rejected the &quot;Technocracy Triumphant&quot; paradigm.<br /> <br /> I would hazard to guess Wraith20 is going to chuck the whole &quot;Charon was really an Angel&quot; development along with the rest of Demon's influences, and Wraith will be better all the for it. Hell, Stygia is going to exist along side of Orpheus in Wraith20... rather than being obliterated by the sixth great Maletstrom, somehow the Underworld is going to have weathered it.<br /> <br /> This is good news, because Revised was the era when while whitewolf put out some of their greatest works... but also had the stupidest cross-overs involving metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those things you describe aren't chucking the metaplot. They are selecting some aspects of metaplot and minimizing them or excising them. That means there is a different metaplot, but there is still metaplot. Or at least intrinsic story built into the setting. And there is pretty much no way that when they expand that &quot;intrinsic story&quot; in further supplements they will also advance it. &quot;Metaplot neutral&quot; gets touted a lot, but, really, can anything related to the original WoD ever be &quot;metaplot neutral&quot;? I doubt it. To shed metaplot entirely, you are going to have to shed the narrative. And that's a large part of what a lot of people who love the CWoD want.<br /> <br /> Prime example already out there: Picking the Nephandi over the Technoracy is a metaplot/narrative decision. There's no way around that. It will be heavily factored into the Technoracy book and the Nephandi book. And those books will have all sorts of info about corrupt Technocrat fuck-ups who have been stepping on their dicks as choreographed to the tune the Nepandi have been playing since the Order of Reason came into being. <br /> <br /> In Wraith, taking out the LGM and making it the MRM (&quot;most recent maelstrom&quot;) or the NM (&quot;No maelstrom here, move along...&quot;) is a decision to chuck the metaplot/narrative of old and insert a new one. Which, of course, they have TO, since there wouldn't be much of a game of WtO if it did happen. And Orpheus is going to have to change substantially to work in a world with no LGM.... As in, &quot;Please ignore fundamental assumptions in books 1 &amp; 2 and pretty much all of 3-5&quot;).<br /> <br /> You can pick and choose what parts of the metaplot play for you. The developers are picking which points play for them. But, for all intents and purposes, the metaplot is OUT there. It's a standing, complicated, contradictory story. I don't think we're going to see much in the way of clear &quot;ignore that BS that connects this to that&quot; based on what we've seen so far. More like &quot;there's some rumors out there that X is connected to Y and that is an option to take, but we're going THIS way with it&quot; or, even more likely (if they are not going to go the Way of Purple Boxes), it won't even be touched on, b/c there is more than enough that's WtO critical to waste word count on it. However, that doesn't obliterate it or excise it. It just ignores it. So, like the cat in the box as seen by an optimistic cat lover, the cat is ALIVE until someone comes along and collapses the waveform. <br /> <br /> Long and short, since they didn't ever say what the Kraken was, it's still a wide-open question. They probably won't. So it's still going to be. They DID say Nhudri was Nhudriel. They probably aren't going to unsay it. Ignore if you hate it or DtF, but it's still out there until countermanded. They did say there was an angel named Charon and the Emperor of Stygia is called Charon. If you hate it, ignore the DtF aspect of it, like you are ignoring the rest of DtF. But, it's still out there until countermanded. <br /> <br /> Remember, there are people out there who love the connections between DtF and whatever as much you love some other connections that you do (like the Triat and the Pattern/Dynamism/Entropy dynamic in Mage). And there are some people that absolutely hate DtF, like you, and there are others who hate those other connections you adore. Since the WoD is presented as a connected narrative as a setting, the connections are there in the abstract totality of the game and you are going to need to invoke the Golden Rule to cut them out. The balance is tipped towards plurality instead of exclusion. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:01:24-07:00","id":563466,"title":"","content":"Seeing as the Sixth Great Maelstrom happened in 1999 and Wraith 20 will be rewinding the timeline to before then, the Orpheus Group went public in 1996 after Project Flatline succeeded earlier that year, so a game where Orpheus crosses over with Wraith is totally doable using the owod as is, if set before the Final Great Maelstrom. This small era of the late 90s is likely where Wraith 20 is going to set and updated around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}